{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1344820-non-werewolves-learning-the-first-tongue","id":1344820,"title":"Non-Werewolves Learning the First Tongue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T20:29:15-07:00","id":1344820,"title":"Non-Werewolves Learning the First Tongue","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I\u2019m aware that humans can, in part, learn the First Tongue, and I remember Blasphemies having rules for it. <br /> <br /> But how do the Uratha feel about a non-werewolf learning the First Tongue? Do the tribes have any specific laws or social mores about teaching the First Tongue to others (even a trusted ally)? Would a werewolf be offended to discover that a human (or other supernatural) knew Uremehir? I didn\u2019t see anything in the book about this. <br /> <br /> Also mechanically, what do you need to take to represent learning the First Tongue in 2e? Assuming I found a teacher, would I simply take the Language Merit? I noticed that members of voyager cults take an Occult Specialty (Spirit Tongues) and that seems to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","user":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","date":". 10-31-2019, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T21:16:09-07:00","id":1344826,"title":"","content":"In second edition you would probably make it a Language Merit, but have some requirements like it has to be taught by a spirit or werewolf, or disadvantages. The human body can't speak the First Tongue very eloquently, it just doesn't have the setup for it.<br /> <br /> There's no specific laws against the language, but as a whole it would probably fall under The Herd Must Not Know, and the general 'don't let humans interfere with the Hisil' stuff. Obviously it would be more acceptable for humans in a pack to do this, otherwise you're looking at someone who is likely going to be a servant for a spirit or become some sort of spirit shaman, and thus trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T21:22:22-07:00","id":1344827,"title":"","content":"It's not offensive, but it's definitely something to pay attention to. First Tongue isn't like, say, Japanese-it's not really something most people who put in the time to learn it would do as a hobby. It's usually a prelude to Some Kind of Occultism that Can Usually Mean Trouble. If a werewolf finds someone using First Tongue, they'll investigate, and based on what they find they'll probably either Hunt Them Into Place or Incorporate Them Into The Pack.<br /> <br /> As for how one does it, you need Opportunity to Learn before, well, learning it, and since it's not exactly the sort of thing that's regularly written down, odds are an individual has done some Occult work/study long before they got enough practice with the language to have it. Figure an Occult 3 and Probably a Specialty'll do it. Supernatural Merits and other Exceptional Circumstances apply, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:18:32-07:00","id":1344876,"title":"","content":"Mechanically speaking I'd just use Multilingual/Language as if it was just another language (except you can never pronounce it perfectly due to human anatomy). The only prerequisite required would be that it makes sense for the character to have that Merit, exactly like all other Merits. I.e. someone taught them First Tongue, and that informs a part of the character's backstory.<br /> <br /> Edit: As such it makes a lot of sense for the character to also have a few dots of Occult, but not a requirement if, for some weird reason, a werewolf taught it to the character without explaining anything about werewolves or spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Multilingual would be much more common than Language. As a second language for Multilingual you could choose either Sumerian or Cuneiform, depending on how the character was taught First Tongue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-31-2019, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:51:13-08:00","id":1346158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1344820-non-werewolves-learning-the-first-tongue?p=1344876#post1344876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically speaking I'd just use Multilingual/Language as if it was just another language (except you can never pronounce it perfectly due to human anatomy). The only prerequisite required would be that it makes sense for the character to have that Merit, exactly like all other Merits. I.e. someone taught them First Tongue, and that informs a part of the character's backstory.<br /> <br /> Edit: As such it makes a lot of sense for the character to also have a few dots of Occult, but not a requirement if, for some weird reason, a werewolf taught it to the character without explaining anything about werewolves or spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Multilingual would be much more common than Language. As a second language for Multilingual you could choose either Sumerian or Cuneiform, depending on how the character was taught First Tongue.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I'm now picturing a Midwestern university basement club gathering to toss 20-siders, chew sliders and practice their &quot;made up&quot; language &quot;just like Tolkien and Klingon!&quot;<br /> <br /> For some reason the members who are best at the language are the luckiest at dice. Odd.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}